    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (81.46) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.59) leading the charge. **Yordan Alvarez** remains the focal point of our offensive production, buoyed by an elite 0.423 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Miller, whose 4.68 xERA suggests plenty of traffic on the basepaths for the middle of the order. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier \"speed-chase\" play; he faces a soft matchup against Ritchie (5.68 xERA) and benefits from an aggressive dynamic platoon edge, making him a critical weapon for our league-leading pursuit of stolen bases. We are also monitoring **Kyle Schwarber** (63.47), whose score is propped up by a significant wind-out benefit and a high-leadoff spot, even as he battles a marginal historical BvP mark against Gray.\n\nTactically, we are leaning into the high-upside speed of **Caleb Durbin** (56.13) and **Luke Raley** (62.83). **Caleb Durbin** manages to maintain a strong efficiency score despite hitting in the #9 hole, largely due to the wind-out conditions and an ideal matchup profile against Painter. **Luke Raley** benefits immensely from the opponent's slow delivery to home plate, which we are heavily weighting in our sprint-speed algorithms to maximize SB opportunities. **Junior Caminero** (58.61) represents a calculated risk today; despite the SP skill disadvantage presented by facing Cease, his placement in the #2 hole and a favorable dynamic platoon split keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Casey Schmitt** (n/a), who remains our primary utility infielder but ultimately failed to crack the top-tier projected efficiency metrics due to the depth of our middle infield today. We prioritized the stolen base ceiling of **Caleb Durbin** over the safer, lower-variance profile of **Casey Schmitt**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Dillon Dingler** (40.89); while he barely clears our marginal threshold, he is currently at risk of falling below our floor if his dynamic platoon disadvantage widens against Scott. With **Trea Turner**, **Christian Yelich**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Gary Sanchez** all confirmed out of their respective lineups, our depth is being tested, but the projected outputs from **Kazuma Okamoto** (43.02) and **Colt Keith** (54.17) provide enough stability to weather the current roster churn.",
